    explanation: "「Vた + 手前」表示「因為已經當著某人的面做了 V，為了顏面／立場上不得不...」。「あげく」是「在多次嘗試後最終...」（結果性，缺「為了立場」這層）；「うえで」是「在做完 V 之後再...」（順序）；「ばかりに」是「就因為...（造成不希望結果）」（負面因果）。本句的「說出口 → 為了面子不能收回」是「手前」典型用法。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Vた + 手前」means \"because I've already done V in front of someone, for the sake of my face / position I have no choice but to...\" 「あげく」means \"after many attempts, finally...\" (a resulting outcome, lacking the \"for the sake of one's standing\" layer); 「うえで」means \"after finishing V, then...\" (sequence); 「ばかりに」means \"simply because... (leading to an unwanted result)\" (negative cause-and-effect). This sentence's \"having said it → can't retract it for face\" is a textbook use of 「手前」." },
