    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Vます stem + つつも」is a literary, written-style \"even though..., still...,\" expressing a gap between awareness and action. 「ながらに」is 「~ながらに」(as in 涙ながらに, etc.), meaning \"in a certain state\" (not concession); 「ものの」also means \"even though..., but...\" but is more colloquial; 「ばかりか」means \"not only..., but even...\" (addition). Here \"lying despite knowing it's wrong\" is a textbook use of 「つつも」, and it attaches perfectly to the ます stem 「知り」." },
