    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Vる + かたわら」is a written-style, long-term parallel meaning \"while doing one's main activity V, one also keeps doing N on the side\" (both are long-term). 「ながら」marks simultaneous actions but on a short time scale (like reading while listening to music); 「うえに」means \"not only..., but also...\" (addition); 「あいだに」means \"during...\" (a time span). Here \"a day job and novel-writing running in parallel over the long term\" is a classic scenario for 「かたわら」." },
