    explanationI18n: { "en": "「N / plain form + ならまだしも」means \"if it's X, that's still somewhat acceptable; but Y goes too far\" (a tolerable/intolerable contrast, with the second clause usually more serious). 「ならいざしらず」is similar but more written; 「とすれば」means \"supposing that\" (a neutral hypothesis); 「といえども」means \"even if\" (concession). Here \"once is fine, but repeatedly is not\" is a classic contrast, and 「ならまだしも」is the most colloquial and natural fit." },
