    explanationI18n: { "en": "「N + のみならず」is a written, discursive \"not only N, but also B...\" (expanding scope). 「ばかりか」is similar but more colloquial and carries a sense of surprise; 「に限らず」also means \"not limited to just N,\" but the nuance is weaker and the second clause is often a parallel example; 「を問わず」means \"regardless of N\" (a regulatory tone). Here the written, argumentative \"not just school, but home too\" fits 「のみならず」best." },
