    explanationI18n: { "en": "\"想像にかたくない\" is a set phrase meaning \"it's not hard to imagine.\" \"にたえない\" means \"so strong that one can't bear it\" or \"not worth watching/listening to.\" \"に忍びない\" means \"can't bring oneself to (do something).\" \"に足る\" means \"worthy of.\" All four are \"に + verb stem\" evaluative patterns, but only \"にかたくない\" pairs with \"想像.\"" },
