    meaningI18n: { "en": "on the contrary" },
    promptLabel: "文章脈絡",
    instructionZh: "短文脈絡：選能讓文章流向自然的接續表現。",
    instructionI18n: { "en": "Passage context: choose the connective that makes the flow of the text natural." },
    promptText: "説明を丁寧にしようとして、担当者は資料に多くの補足を加えた。情報量は増えたものの、中心となる論点が見えにくくなった。___、参加者からは「前より分かりにくい」との声も出た。",
    promptContextZh: "為了把說明做得更仔細，承辦人在資料裡加入了許多補充。資訊量雖然增加了，核心的論點卻變得難以看清。反倒是，參加者之間還出現了「比以前更難懂」的聲音。",
    promptContextI18n: { "en": "In an effort to make the explanation more thorough, the person in charge added many supplementary notes to the materials. Although the amount of information increased, the central point became harder to see. On the contrary, some participants even said it was \"harder to understand than before.\"" },
    hintZh: "改善意圖與實際效果之間出現落差。",
    hintI18n: { "en": "A gap appears between the intention to improve and the actual effect." },
    expectedAnswer: "かえって",
    options: ["かえって","したがって","加えて","同時に"],
    explanation: "「かえって」表示結果與原本意圖或預期相反。「したがって」是順向結論；「加えて」是追加同方向資訊；「同時に」表示並行。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "\"かえって\" indicates that the result is the opposite of the original intention or expectation. \"したがって\" introduces a conclusion in the same direction. \"加えて\" adds information in the same direction. \"同時に\" indicates something happening in parallel." },
