    explanation: "「N + のこととて」是書面謙恭的「因為是…（故有不足，請體諒）」，本句「因屬初次嘗試而請見諒」即此。「にかこつけて」是「假借…為藉口」（負面）；「であれ」是「無論是…」（讓步）；「にいたって」是「到了…地步才…」（遲來反應）。只有「のこととて」契合致歉、求諒的鄭重語境。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "「N + のこととて」 is the written, humble \"since it is... (hence the shortcomings, please bear with us),\" and this sentence—asking forgiveness because it is a first attempt—is exactly that. 「にかこつけて」 means \"using... as a pretext\" (negative); 「であれ」 means \"whatever/no matter...\" (concession); 「にいたって」 means \"only when it reached the point of...\" (a belated reaction). Only のこととて fits this formal context of apologizing and asking for understanding." },
