    explanationI18n: { "en": "「ともすれば」 expresses a tendency to slip in a certain direction if one isn't careful, with the following clause pairing with 「〜やすい」; here 「偏りやすい」 follows most naturally. 「とはいえ」 is a concession; 「一方で」 contrasts the other side; 「なお」 adds supplementary information—none of them link up with 「やすい」." },
