    explanationI18n: { "en": "When attaching to a noun, the form is 「Nのかたわら」, meaning \"holding that role as one's main job while pursuing another activity long-term alongside it.\" 「のがてら」 fails on both grammar and nuance (がてら mostly attaches to action nouns to mean doing something on the way); 「に際して」 means \"on the occasion of...\" (a point in time); 「を皮切りに」 means \"starting with...\" (a starting point). This sentence describes a long-term parallel activity, so のかたわら is the choice." },
