    explanationI18n: { "en": "「N + にあるまじき + N」 means \"a... that someone of that standing should absolutely never do (a harsh condemnation),\" often paired with nouns for public figures, politicians, teachers, and the like; here condemning a politician's improper statement fits perfectly. 「ともなれば」 means \"once one becomes..., it naturally follows that...\" (a conditional inference, not condemnation); 「ならではの」 means \"unique to... (a positive distinction)\"; 「をものともしない」 means \"heedless of... (undaunted by difficulty).\" None of the three work in this sentence; only にあるまじき expresses condemnation of failing the duties of one's role." },
