    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer 「介護にかまけて」 means being so consumed by caring for the grandfather that one leaves one's own health checkup neglected for a long time; the sentence clearly has a neglected item. 「をめぐって」 marks issues or disputes surrounding the caregiving and wouldn't naturally lead to postponing the checkup. 「に応じて」 means in accordance with or in response to the caregiving situation and can't account for neglecting one's own checkup. 「にもまして」 means even more than the caregiving, and followed by 「先延ばしにしていた」 the meaning doesn't hold." },
