    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Aから Bに至るまで」means \"extending from A all the way to B (with even B being no exception).\" The sentence, \"even individual shops, all the way from large corporations, were hit,\" uses 個人商店に至るまで to convey how comprehensively the damage spread. をもって means \"by means of ~ / as of ~ (a point in time),\" and \"as of an individual shop\" makes no sense. によって means \"by / due to ~\" and can't form a range with から. において means \"in (a place/field)\" and can't pair with から to form a range. Only に至るまで can pair with から to express \"reaching all the way to the far extreme.\"" },
