    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Vない＋でもない」means \"not that it isn't ~ (a reserved acknowledgment, somewhat understandable).\" っこない means \"absolutely impossible to ~\" (理解できっこない = completely impossible to understand — the opposite meaning); ようがない means \"there's no way to ~\" (attaches to the ます-stem: 理解しようがない); まい means \"probably won't ~.\" Only ないでもない expresses \"it's not entirely impossible to understand.\"" },
