    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is \"というに足りない.\" Attached to a noun, it means \"not yet enough to be called…\"; here it says that changing just one date is not enough to be called a 『改訂 (revision)』. \"にほかならない\" means \"is precisely / is nothing other than…,\" a strong affirmation that it is indeed a 『改訂』; but declaring that changing a single date 『is precisely a revision』 is clearly excessive and contradicts 『doesn't count as a revision』. \"を招きかねない\" means 『might bring about…』, but 『bringing about a revision』 does not fit the sentence. \"を隠しきれない\" means 『cannot be fully hidden』, but there is no intent to hide a revision here, so it does not hold up." },
