    explanationI18n: { "en": "\"(この／ここ) + period + というもの\" means \"(throughout this period) constantly…,\" followed by a continuing state. \"ここしばらくというもの、彼女は会議で一言も発していない\" means \"for a while now, she hasn't said a single word in meetings,\" so it is correct. \"だというのに\" (even though…) is adversative and cannot simply carry a continuing state. \"にかけて\" (over the range from… to…, as in 春から夏にかけて) is unnatural after \"ここしばらく.\" \"にしても\" (even if…) expresses concession, which does not fit a simple statement of a continuing state. Only \"というもの\" can express \"(throughout this period) constantly….\"" },
