    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is \"に至っても.\" \"正式通告に至っても\" means \"even having reached the stage of formal notice, (he) still…,\" echoing the following \"なお.\" \"にあたって\" indicates preparation, care, or timing when undertaking something, and cannot express the adversative \"even so, still.\" \"をもって\" indicates means, a deadline, or a dividing point, which would make it \"using formal notice as a boundary or basis\" — not fitting the sense of still demanding changes to the terms. \"に先立って\" means \"prior to,\" which would make it action before the formal notice, unlike the context of still not changing even after reaching the notice stage." },
