    explanationI18n: { "en": "「Vます-stem + つ + (antonym) Vます-stem + つ」 is a fixed paired-action pattern, and 「行きつ戻りつ」 is an idiom (pacing to and fro, walking back and forth) that matches the hesitant situation of 「答えを出せず…ため息ばかり」, so it is correct. 「行くや戻るや」 (the や〜や pattern isn't this paired idiom, and the connection is also wrong), 「行くと戻ると」 (the と〜と pattern is parallel listing, not \"back and forth\"), and 「行きや戻りや」 are none of them the established 「〜つ〜つ」 form and can't express going back and forth. Only 「行きつ戻りつ」 is the correct idiom." },
