    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer 「逆襲（ぎゃくしゅう）」means switching from defense to offense and striking back handsomely, echoing the context of refusing to give up and showing a transformed self. 「降伏」means to surrender and submit, the opposite of 「泣いて終わるつもりはない」; 「退散」means to disperse or clear out, a retreat rather than an attack; 「撤退」means to withdraw troops and pull back, likewise a retreat, not an advance. Only 「逆襲」carries the meaning of an active counterattack, making it the sole correct answer." },
