    explanationI18n: { "en": "The sentence explicitly states 「幼いころから毎日のように一緒に遊んだ」(played together almost every day since childhood), pinning down 「幼なじみ」(childhood friend), someone who grew up alongside you. 「他人」means a complete stranger, which directly contradicts having played together daily since childhood; 「恋人」means a lover, but the sentence only describes playing together since childhood with no romantic relationship, so it doesn't fit; 「先輩」means a senior or upperclassman, a hierarchical, seniority-based relationship that doesn't match a friendship between peers who grew up together. The only correct answer is 「幼なじみ」." },
