    promptLabel: "詞彙填空",
    instructionZh: "句中填空：選最自然的詞語。",
    instructionI18n: { "en": "Fill in the blank: choose the most natural word." },
    promptText: "あの日交わした約束だけを支えに、いつか君と___できる日を信じて、私はこの街で待ち続けている。",
    promptContextZh: "我僅憑那天彼此許下的約定支撐著，相信總有一天能與你再會，在這座城市裡持續守候。",
    promptContextI18n: { "en": "Sustained only by the promise we made that day, believing in the day I can meet you again, I keep waiting here in this city." },
    hintZh: "多年前與某個重要的人分別後立下約定，如今獨自留在這座城裡，把那個約定當成唯一的支撐，深信約定實現的那一天總會到來。",
    hintI18n: { "en": "Years ago, after parting from someone important, she made a promise; now she stays alone in this city, treating that promise as her only support and firmly believing the day it comes true will surely arrive." },
    expectedAnswer: "再会",
    options: ["再会", "再開", "再現", "再生"],
    explanation: "「再会」指與人再次相見、重逢，正符合「いつか君と___できる日」這種與心上人重逢的語境，唯一成立。「再開（さいかい）」雖同音，但指中斷的活動或營業重新開始，對象不是人，代入不成立。「再現」指事物景象再度出現、重現，搭配「君と」不自然。「再生」指重生、復原或播放（影音）等，與「與某人相見」無關。三個干擾在此語境皆明確不成立，故答案唯一為「再会」。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "「再会」means meeting a person again, a reunion, which fits the context of 「いつか君と___できる日」(the day I can meet you again) with a loved one, and is the only word that works. 「再開（さいかい）」is a homophone but refers to a suspended activity or business resuming, not a person, so it doesn't fit. 「再現」means a thing or scene appearing again, a reenactment, which is unnatural with 「君と」. 「再生」means rebirth, restoration, or playback (of audio/video), unrelated to meeting a person. All three distractors clearly fail in this context, so the sole correct answer is 「再会」." },
