    explanationI18n: { "en": "焦がす is read こがす, meaning 'to scorch, to burn.' Here it paints a summer image of the noon sun searing the skin hot. All four options keep the same ending okurigana 「〜がす」 and set their traps only on the sound and voicing of 「焦」: ごがす wrongly voices the first syllable 「こ」 into 「ご」; こがず wrongly voices the final 「す」 into 「ず」; くがす misreads the first syllable 「こ」 as 「く」. None of these is the correct reading, so the only correct answer is こがす." },
    exampleJapanese: "真上から照りつける正午の日差しが、僕の素肌をじりじりと焦がすほど、夏の鼓動が熱く高鳴っていた。",
    exampleMeaningZh: "從正上方直射而下的正午陽光,熱得幾乎要把我的肌膚烤焦,夏天的心跳也滾燙地高鳴著。"
