    explanationI18n: { "en": "心底 (しんそこ) means from the deepest part of one's heart, from genuine feeling, fitting the context of 'truly feeling alive.' 目先 means the immediate, short-sighted moment, which doesn't fit the profound feeling of 「生きていると感じた」; 上辺 means the surface, the outward appearance, the opposite of coming from within; 建前 means one's stated position or lip service, the opposite of genuine feeling. So the only correct answer is 心底." },
