    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 無常. From flowers that scatter as soon as they bloom, the sentence expresses the reflection that 'all things in the world change and nothing stays the same.' 無理 means unreasonable or difficult, 無効 means without effect, and 無口 means a quiet, reticent nature — none fits the context of transience in 「世の___を感じる」, so they don't hold up." },
