    explanation: "正解「察するにかたくない」是固定搭配，前接『察する』這類推測動詞語幹，表示『他人的心境一想便能體會』，貼合老粉得知偶像畢業時的失落。「にあるまじき」是『身為某身分不該有的（譴責）』，需前接身分名詞並修飾後項名詞，此處『察する』為動詞、句中也無被指責的言行，接續與語意皆不合。「にたえない」是『不堪～』，要前接『見る／聞く』或感情名詞（如『見るにたえない』『遺憾にたえない』），接在『察する』後既不搭配、也不表『不難體會』之意。「にすぎない」是『只不過』，用於縮小評價，接在『察する』後不成句，更與『心情可輕易設想』的句意相反。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer 「察するにかたくない」is a fixed collocation: preceded by the stem of an inference verb like 察する, it means 'one can readily grasp how another feels just by thinking about it' — fitting the veteran fans' loss upon learning of the idol's graduation. 「にあるまじき」means 'unbecoming of a certain role (censure),' requiring a preceding role noun and modifying a following noun; here 察する is a verb and there is no reproachable conduct in the sentence, so both the connection and the meaning are off. 「にたえない」means 'unbearable to ~,' requiring a preceding 見る／聞く or an emotion noun (e.g., 「見るにたえない」「遺憾にたえない」); attaching it to 察する is neither a valid collocation nor does it convey 'not hard to understand.' 「にすぎない」means 'is nothing more than,' used to diminish; attaching it to 察する forms no valid sentence and further contradicts the sense that the feelings are easily surmised." },
