    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「にひきかえ」. The first term 'the old workplace, overtime and no leave' and the second term 'the current company, leaving on time and free leave' are two jobs in sharp contrast, each with a good-or-bad evaluation (bad / good) — exactly this usage. 「にもまして」 means 'even more than...,' a same-direction increase (as in 「前の職場にもまして残業が多い」), which doesn't match the positive-negative gap here, so it can't be used. 「反面」 is for two sides of the same subject (「給料が高い反面、激務だ」 refers to two sides of one job), but here it's a comparison of two different jobs — different subjects — so it can't be used. 「とともに」 means 'along with / together with,' an accompanying relation, and can't form a natural clause with 「それ」 or express an opposing contrast, so it can't be used." },
