    hintI18n: { "en": "Before the blank is the i-adjective 「狭い」. Choose a conjunctive (連用) form that attaches directly to an i-adjective, binds 'X' and the positive evaluation that follows into a single descriptive sentence, and expresses adversative concession. One option only attaches to the verb ます-form and breaks with 「狭い」; another can only serve as a sentence-level conjunction requiring a full preceding clause or だ／である, so it can't cling to an adjective as a mid-sentence conjunctive the way this item needs." },
