    explanation: "正解是「だけに」：前項『被視為奪冠熱門』這份高評價，正因如此讓後項的『悔しさ』程度更深，貼合『正因前項而後項更甚』。「とあって」表特殊客觀情況→自然結果、偏報導敘事語氣，與此處主觀情感『悔しさは大きかった』的加深不相稱。「にしては」表『以…而言卻出乎意料』的落差，雖然首輪出局確實意外，但句子要表達的是因被看好而懊惱更深，而非評價與表現的落差本身，焦點不符。「ばかりに」表『就因為…招致了某一壞結果』，後項應是被招來的不幸事態，而此處後項是情感程度的加深，並非被前因招致的災禍，故不成立。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「だけに」: the earlier clause — the high esteem of being seen as a favorite to win — is precisely what makes the 『悔しさ』 in the second clause all the deeper, fitting 'precisely because of the first clause, the second is all the more so.' 「とあって」 marks a special objective circumstance leading to a natural result with a reportorial, narrative tone, which does not match the deepening of subjective emotion (『悔しさは大きかった』) here. 「にしては」 expresses the gap of 'unexpectedly, for a ~'; although a first-round exit is indeed a surprise, what the sentence expresses is deeper chagrin because she was favored, not the gap between reputation and performance itself, so the focus does not match. 「ばかりに」 means 'just because of ~, a bad result was brought about,' where the second clause should be an invited misfortune; here the second clause is a deepening of emotional degree, not a disaster brought about by the cause, so it does not work." },
