    hintZh: "這是記者客觀報導的口吻：前面陳述一個眾所周知的場合事實，後面只是平鋪直敘那因此而來、理所當然的熱鬧光景，沒有任何說話者的感慨或評價。",
    hintI18n: { "en": "This is a reporter's objective, reportorial voice: the first part states a widely known fact about the occasion, and the second simply describes, matter-of-factly, the naturally resulting bustle, with no emotion or evaluation from the speaker." },
    expectedAnswer: "とあって",
    options: ["とあって", "だけに", "ともなれば", "とあれば"],
    explanation: "正解是「とあって」：前項「今年最後の花火大会」是一個客觀的場合事實，後項「会場は朝から大勢の見物客で賑わっていた」是因此自然出現的熱鬧現象。配合句首「取材に訪れた記者によると」與句尾「という」的傳聞報導框架，全句是純粹轉述他人觀察到的客觀景象，正是「とあって」典型的新聞報導語體（特殊場合→理所當然的結果），完全契合。「だけに」雖也表原因，但帶有說話者本人「正因為…所以更…」的主觀強調與評價，後項多接情感或感慨；本句既是記者轉述的客觀光景、又無任何評價語氣，與「だけに」的評價性主觀立場不合。「ともなれば」是「一旦到了／成為…就」的假設語氣，但本句後項是已經發生的過去事實（賑わっていた），與假設不合。「とあれば」是「若是為了…的話」的條件假設，後項通常接決意或讓步，與「實際已經很熱鬧」的既成事實矛盾，故不成立。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「とあって」: the first clause 「今年最後の花火大会」 is an objective fact about the occasion, and the second 「会場は朝から大勢の見物客で賑わっていた」 is the bustle that naturally results from it. Combined with the hearsay-reporting frame of 「取材に訪れた記者によると」 at the start and 「という」 at the end, the whole sentence purely relays an objective scene observed by others — exactly the news-reporting register typical of 「とあって」 (special occasion → its natural result), a perfect fit. 「だけに」 also marks a cause, but carries the speaker's own subjective emphasis and evaluation of 'precisely because ~, all the more ~,' with the second clause usually taking emotion or sentiment; this sentence is an objective scene relayed by a reporter with no evaluative tone, so it does not fit 「だけに」's evaluative, subjective stance. 「ともなれば」 is the hypothetical 'once it comes to / becomes ~,' but here the second clause is an already-completed past fact (賑わっていた), which does not fit a hypothesis. 「とあれば」 is the conditional 'if it is for the sake of ~,' usually followed by resolve or concession, contradicting the established fact that it was 'already bustling,' so it does not work." },
