    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「とあって」: the first clause 「数十年に一度の皆既日食が見られる」 is an extremely special, rare situation (an objective fact), and the second 「世界中から観光客が押し寄せた」 is the crowd phenomenon that naturally occurs as a result (an objective description), fitting 'because of some special circumstance → naturally leading to the second clause.' 「だけに」 means 'precisely because ~, all the deeper,' with the second clause usually taking emotion or evaluation, which does not fit well with this sentence's plain, objective description of tourists flooding in. 「ともなれば」 is the hypothetical 'once it comes to ~,' but the second clause is an already-occurred past fact (押し寄せた), not a conjecture, so it does not fit. 「とあれば」 is the conditional 'if it is for the sake of ~,' with the second clause expected to take resolve or concession (e.g. 「どんな遠方でも行く」), contradicting this statement of an established fact that crowds have flooded in, so it does not work." },
