    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「そばから」: the sentence's 「片付けた…また散らかす」 and 「いつまでもきれいにならない」 depict tidying and messing up over and over, repeatedly canceling out in vain — exactly 「そばから」's core meaning of 'no sooner is the first done than the second happens again and cancels it out, fruitlessly repeated.' The distractor 「や否や」 means a one-time 'as soon as ~,' describing a single instantaneous sequence with no sense of repeated futility, which does not fit the cyclical context of 「また…ので、いつまでも…ない」. The distractor 「たとたん」 means a one-time, instantaneous 'the moment ~,' often with surprise, and cannot express repeated back-and-forth; inserting it leaves only a one-off event, clashing with 「また」. The distractor 「が早いか」 is likewise a one-time 'the instant ~, right away,' stressing near-simultaneous actions, with no sense of repeated canceling-out, and cannot carry the long-term cycle implied by 「いつまでもきれいにならない」." },
