    explanationI18n: { "en": "「dictionary-form verb ＋だに」 is a literary emphasis meaning 'merely doing the first action (imagining, hearing, etc.) is already this much,' and this sentence 「想像する＋___＋身の毛がよだつ」 is exactly that pattern, so 「だに」 works. 「すら」 and 「さえ」 both mean 'even ~,' but must attach to a noun (＋case particle) and cannot directly attach to a dictionary-form verb — 「想像するすら」/「想像するさえ」 do not connect. 「まで」 means 'even to the extent of ~,' and likewise must attach to a noun or clause; attached to the dictionary form 「想像するまで」 it becomes an enumerative nuance of 'even to the point of imagining,' which cannot carry the instantaneous, intense reaction of 「身の毛がよだつ」, so it does not fit. Only 「だに」 locks in the single answer." },
