    hintI18n: { "en": "The subject is the 'work,' and what follows must express that it inevitably causes the 'other party — the viewers' to have a certain reaction; it is not the speaker being unable to help themselves, nor being forced to have no choice." },
    expectedAnswer: "ずにはおかない",
    options: ["ずにはおかない", "ずにはいられない", "ざるをえない", "ないではいられない"],
    explanation: "正解是「ずにはおかない」。主語為作品（見る者を涙させる），表示這部作品基於其感染力必定使他者（觀眾）產生流淚這一反應，符合『作品／事件必定使對方陷入某狀態』的使役致果用法。「ずにはいられない」表示說話者自身情不自禁（如『泣かずにはいられない＝我忍不住哭』），主語必須是有情感的人、而非作品，且這裡的對象是「他者」而非說話者，故不成立。「ざるをえない」意為被外在情勢逼迫「不得不～」（如『認めざるをえない』），與「使對方流淚」的致果語意完全不符。「ないではいられない」同樣是說話者本人忍不住要做某事，主語是人的自發情感，無法承接「涙させ（使他人流淚）」這種使役致果。因此四選項代入後只有「ずにはおかない」成立。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「ずにはおかない」. The subject is the work (見る者を涙させる), expressing that by its power the work inevitably makes the other party (the viewers) react by crying, fitting the causative-effect usage 'a work / event inevitably drives the other party into some state.' 「ずにはいられない」 expresses the speaker's own inability to help themselves (e.g. 『泣かずにはいられない＝I can't help crying』), and its subject must be a person with feelings, not a work, and here the object is 'the other party' rather than the speaker, so it does not work. 「ざるをえない」 means being forced by external circumstances to 'have no choice but to ~' (e.g. 『認めざるをえない』), completely mismatching the effect-inducing meaning of 'making the other party cry.' 「ないではいられない」 is likewise the speaker themselves unable to keep from doing something, with a person's spontaneous emotion as subject, and cannot carry the causative effect 「涙させ (making others cry)」. Therefore, of the four options only 「ずにはおかない」 works." },
