    explanationI18n: { "en": "The correct answer is 「ずにはおかない」. The subject is 「不正の発覚（an event）」, and 「株主たちを怒らせる」 expresses that this event inevitably throws the other party (the shareholders) into anger — a natural effect of 'an event inevitably making the other party react,' which also pairs naturally with 「だろう」 for conjecture. 「ずにはすまない」 expresses that morally or reasonably the speaker themselves must do something (e.g. 『謝らずにはすまない＝it won't do not to apologize』), with a responsible person as subject and an action they themselves must take, and cannot carry the other-directed effect of 'making the shareholders angry.' 「ざるをえない」 means being forced by circumstances to 'have no choice but to ~,' describing the subject's own forced choice rather than making others react, so it does not fit. 「ずにはいられない」 is the speaker's own uncontainable emotion (subject a person), but here the object of the anger is the shareholders, not the speaker, and the subject is an event, so it does not work. Only 「ずにはおかない」 works." },
