    explanation: "正解是「とあれば」：表示『若是為了女兒的盛裝身影這個特別目的的話』，平常出無精的父親也願意破例遠行，符合假定且「不惜」的語氣，與後句「喜んで足を運んだ」呼應。「とあって」表既成事實的特殊原因（由於…自然出現的結果、報導語氣），但前句是『為了看…』的目的假定而非已發生的事實，且帶有破例願為的轉折，不合。「ともなれば」表『一旦到了／成為某狀況就必然…』，需接時期或身分等狀況性名詞，這裡是個人目的而非必然狀況，不成立。「にしては」表『以…而言卻…』的逆評價，無法承接『為了…的話就願意』的假定願為語意，故不對。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「とあれば」: it means 『if it's for the special purpose of seeing his daughter in her finery』, so even a father who hates going out will make an exception and travel far, fitting a supposition with the nuance of 『won't hesitate』 and echoing the following clause 「喜んで足を運んだ」. 「とあって」 states a special cause that is an accomplished fact (a naturally arising result, with a reportorial tone), but the preceding clause is a purpose-based supposition 『in order to see…』 rather than something that has happened, and it carries the twist of exceptionally being willing, so it doesn't fit. 「ともなれば」 means 『once it reaches/becomes a certain state, then inevitably…』 and must attach to a situational noun such as a time period or status; here it is a personal purpose, not an inevitable situation, so it does not hold. 「にしては」 expresses the counter-evaluation 『for…, yet…』 and cannot pick up the hypothetical-willingness sense of 『if it's for…, then one is willing』, so it is wrong." },
