    explanation: "正解是「をものともせず」：前接「度重なる手術と長い闘病生活」這類嚴峻逆境，後接主語自己「夢を諦めずに努力し続けた」的正面奮進行動，正是「不畏艱難、勇往直前」的典型用法。「をよそに」=無視旁人的擔心/關心/期待（含不顧旁人感受的自私語感），但這裡受詞是自身遭遇的病痛逆境、非他人的關心，且主語是積極克服而非冷漠無視，語感不合。「にもかかわらず」=儘管～卻～，只是逆接陳述事實，缺少「把困難不當回事、主動奮起克服」的積極語感，且須直接接體言或常體句、與此處勇進語氣不符。「を余儀なくされ」=被迫不得不（被動接受不情願的結果），與後文主語主動堅持、努力到底的積極行動完全相反，故不可填入。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「をものともせず」: it takes a harsh adversity like 「度重なる手術と長い闘病生活」 in front and the subject's own positive, forging-ahead action 「夢を諦めずに努力し続けた」 behind — exactly the classic usage 『undaunted by hardship, pressing forward bravely』. 「をよそに」 = ignoring others' worry/concern/expectations (with a selfish nuance of disregarding others' feelings), but here the object is her own affliction and adversity, not others' concern, and the subject actively overcomes rather than coldly ignores, so the nuance doesn't fit. 「にもかかわらず」 = although ～, yet ～, merely a concessive statement of fact, lacking the active nuance of 『treating the difficulty as nothing and rising to overcome it』; it also must attach directly to a noun or plain-form clause and doesn't match the courageous tone here. 「を余儀なくされ」 = be forced to, have no choice but to (passively accepting an unwanted result), which is the exact opposite of the subject's active persistence and effort to the end in the following text, so it cannot fill the blank." },
