    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「ずくめ」. This sentence, with 「どの一皿も例外なく」 and 「一切手抜きのない」, locks in the positive context 『every dish, without exception, uniformly excellent』, exactly fitting the sense of 「ずくめ」 as 『uniform throughout, all the same from start to finish』, and it matches perfectly the overall praise of 「高級店だけあって…大満足」. 「ばかり」 means 『nothing but, over-weighted toward one thing while excluding others』, stressing a biased contrast (as in 「肉ばかり食べる」, complaining about eating only one kind), and it cannot support a description like 「どの一皿も例外なく」 of 『no exceptions, uniform throughout』 — since the sentence already states every dish is excellent with no exception, there are no 『other, excluded options』 that 「ばかり」 implies, so it clashes with the 『all uniform, satisfying』 tone here. 「だらけ」 means messily covered in something, mostly for negative or troublesome things (間違いだらけ・ほこりだらけ), so 「ごちそうだらけ」 would give the odd nuance of complaining that there's too much rich food in a jumble, which doesn't fit the positive sense. 「まみれ」 can only attach to liquids or powders smeared on a surface (汗まみれ・泥まみれ・血まみれ), so 「ごちそうまみれ」 doesn't work, because dishes aren't something smeared on the body." },
