    explanation: "正解是「ところで」：與副詞「いくら」呼應，前接動詞た形「取り替えた」，後接「もう…動かないだろう」，表「即使更換再多零件也是徒勞」，正是本文法「做了也無濟於事」的用法。「からには」意為「既然…」，後須接理所當然的行動或決心，無法與「動かない」的徒勞否定搭配。「ばかりに」意為「就因為…才（招致不好結果）」，強調單一原因導致後果，但句中換零件並非導致機器壞掉的原因，語意不合。「ものなら」表「如果能…的話」的假定願望，須接可能形，接過去式「取り替えた」且後句為否定推測時不成立。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「ところで」: echoing the adverb 「いくら」, attaching to the ta-form verb 「取り替えた」, and followed by 「もう…動かないだろう」, it expresses that 'no matter how many parts you replace, it's futile' — exactly this grammar's 'doing it is no use' usage. 「からには」 means 'now that…' and must be followed by a matter-of-course action or resolve, so it cannot pair with the futile negation 「動かない」. 「ばかりに」 means 'simply because… (bringing about a bad result)', emphasizing a single cause leading to a consequence, but replacing parts isn't what broke the machine, so it doesn't fit. 「ものなら」 expresses the hypothetical wish 'if only I could…' and must take the potential form, so it doesn't work following the past form 「取り替えた」 with a negative conjecture in the latter clause." },
