    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「やら」: paired with 「挨拶するやら」 in the following clause, it forms the jumbled listing 「AやらBやらで、大変だ」, setting 'picking out furniture' and 'greeting the neighbors' side by side into a 'what with… and…' sense of hectic busyness, followed by 「大変だ」, so only it works. 「なり」 = 「AなりBなり」 means choose one of two to do (either-or), which cannot pair with the fixed 「やら」 already there and carries a choosing rather than a listing sense; 「つつ」 = 'while…' only means two actions happening at once with no 'multiple jumbled items' sense, and is hard to echo the following 「やら」; 「がてら」 = 'while also (doing something else in passing)' expresses a secondary purpose (e.g. 「散歩がてら」), cannot pair with 「やら」 to form a listing, and makes no sense here." },
