    explanationI18n: { "en": "Correct answer 「と相まって」: the night view and the clear air interact with each other, raising the appeal 'all the more.' This fits 'A and B intertwine to produce a multiplied result.' 「に伴って」 expresses a one-directional change that moves in step with something (as in 「成長に伴って」 'as one grows'); here the two are not in a leading-and-following relationship, so it doesn't work. 「とともに」 means 'together with / as…,' merely juxtaposition or simultaneity; it lacks the nuance of 'acting on each other to amplify the effect' and does not suit the multiplying context of 「一層魅了」. 「に加えて」 is a simple addition, 'on top of…, add…'; the two are merely summed rather than mutually generative, so it cannot express a multiplied effect." },
