    explanationI18n: { "en": "Correct answer 「と相まって」: the scenery and the hospitality mirror each other and blend, and 「初めて生まれる独特の魅力」 'a distinctive charm that arises only then' makes explicit that this is a multiplied result produced only after the two interact—exactly the multiplying nuance of 「と相まって」. 「に伴って」 expresses a change that follows in step with something (as in 「観光客の増加に伴って」 'as tourists increase'), but the two here are not a leading-and-following change, and attaching it to 「初めて生まれる」 doesn't work, so it fails. 「とともに」 only expresses juxtaposition or simultaneity and cannot convey the mutually reinforcing cause of 'only through the two blending does the charm first emerge,' so the nuance is insufficient. 「に加えて」 is a mere additive 'on top of that,' with elements simply summed rather than intertwining and co-arising, which contradicts the interactive, generative effect stressed by 「と相まって…初めて生まれる」, so it fails." },
