    options: ["に即して", "に沿って", "に応じて", "において"],
    explanation: "正解是「に即して」。前接「客観的なデータ」這種現場確認、已成定局的客觀資料，表示緊貼著該既成內容、不摻臆測地逐一檢證，正合語境。「に沿って」表順著抽象的方針/路線/計畫/期待去做，客觀資料是查證的依憑而非要遵循的方針，故不合。「に応じて」表因應對象的變化而各自對應（如年齢に応じて、状況に応じて），句中資料是固定不變的既成內容、沒有隨之變動的對象，不合。「において」表「在～（場合/領域/時間點）」，「データにおいて」只標示場所或範疇，無法表達「緊貼資料去查證」之意，語意不通。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「に即して」. It follows 「客観的なデータ」, objective data confirmed on site and already settled as fact, and means keeping close to that established content, verifying item by item without mixing in conjecture—exactly right for the context. 「に沿って」 means acting along an abstract policy/course/plan/expectation; objective data is the basis one verifies against, not a policy to follow, so it doesn't fit. 「に応じて」 means responding individually to changes in the object (as in 「年齢に応じて」 or 「状況に応じて」); here the data is fixed, established content with no varying object to respond to, so it doesn't fit. 「において」 means 'in ~ (a setting/domain/point in time)'; 「データにおいて」 only marks a place or domain and cannot express 'verifying by hugging the data closely,' so the meaning doesn't come through." },
