    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is 「に即して」. It follows 「条文の文言」 (the literal wording of the statute), a fixed, established textual standard, and means judging strictly in accordance with (hugging) that wording itself, word for word. This fits perfectly with 「改正のない」 'unrevised' and 「一字一句厳密に」 'strictly, word for word.' 「に応じて」 means responding individually to changes in an object and adjusting accordingly, but the sentence has already locked the standard in place with 「改正のない」, leaving no 'change to respond to,' so it doesn't work. 「に沿って」 means going along a policy, expectation, or general direction; its nuance is looser and allows flexible interpretation within that direction, which clashes with 「一字一句厳密に」 'word for word, hugging the literal text,' so it fails. 「にひきかえ」 means 'in contrast to ~,' a contrastive usage, and is completely off in meaning." },
