    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is「ながらも」.「新人」is a noun and can directly take ながらも, giving the concessive meaning 'a newcomer though she was, she performed outstandingly', which naturally sets up the contrast with the following『誰よりも早く把握してみせた』.「ものを」means 'even though… (but did the opposite / didn't do it)', carrying reproach or regret, and is mostly used at the end of a sentence for something contrary to fact; here we're praising her excellent performance, so the meaning is opposite.「つつ」must attach to a verb's ます-stem and cannot attach to the noun「新人」, a fatal grammatical mismatch.「ばかりに」means 'just because… it brought about a bad result' and must be followed by a negative outcome, but here it's followed by a positive achievement, so it doesn't fit." },
