    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is「に至って」: the deterioration worsened steadily and accumulated to the extreme point of the ceiling collapsing, and the following clause『ようやく…予算を組んだ』echoes 'only when it got this bad did they finally', a seamless contextual fit.「に先立って」means 'prior to…', the opposite direction—the budgeting came after the collapse—which clashes with「ようやく」, so it doesn't work.「にあたって」means 'on the occasion of…' and only marks a neutral point in time, lacking the 'only after worsening to an extreme' turn and the 'at last' sense, so it can't take up「ようやく」and is wrong.「に応じて」means 'in accordance with / along with…' and needs a basis that varies correspondingly; it's unnatural attached to a clause like『崩れ落ちる』that reaches a critical point, and can't express 'at last', so it's incorrect." },
