    explanation: "正解是「だけに」：前項「費盡辛勞栽培」是原因，正因為投入心力多，後項採收的喜悅才隨之加倍，貼合『正因為前項所以程度更深』。「とあって」用於由特殊客觀狀況自然導出某結果（如『連假とあって混雑した』），重點在客觀因果而非情感程度的加深，代入後無法承接「喜びはひとしおだった」的層次感。「にしては」表示與前項標準相比出現意外落差，但句中並非要說「以辛苦栽培的菜而言喜悅卻意外地…」，而是強調喜悅更深，故不合。「ものだから」用於說明、辯解某結果的原因（帶主觀緣由口吻），無法表達「因此情感程度更深一層」的遞進，語感不自然。",
    explanationI18n: { "en": "The answer is「だけに」: the first clause 'grown with great effort' is the cause, and precisely because so much effort went in, the joy of harvest in the second clause is doubled, fitting 'precisely because of the first clause, the degree is deeper'.「とあって」is used when a special objective situation naturally leads to some result (e.g.『連休とあって混雑した』), focusing on objective causation rather than a deepening of emotional degree, so it can't take up the layered feeling of『喜びはひとしおだった』.「にしては」indicates an unexpected gap compared to the standard of the first clause, but the sentence isn't saying 'for vegetables grown with such effort, the joy was unexpectedly…'; it's emphasizing that the joy is deeper, so it doesn't fit.「ものだから」is used to explain or justify the cause of some result (with a subjective, excusing tone) and can't express the escalation of 'therefore the emotional degree deepens a notch', so it reads unnaturally." },
